; claude: PostScript (John Warnock and Chuck Geschke, Adobe, 1984): a
; page described as a program -- Ps_lexer (the tokens), Ps_graphics
; (the current transformation matrix, paths, arcs as Beziers, curves
; flattened), Ps_machine (the operand, dictionary and execution stacks,
; the operators, a step at a time), Ps_disk (programs to run). Run by
; TinyPostScript (apps/graphics/).
;
; No Playground and no font (languages/README.md): the letters' strokes
; are the host's, a function the caller gives. In the package
; tiny_languages, as tiny_languages.postscript.
(library
 (name postscript)
 (public_name tiny_languages.postscript)
 (wrapped false)
)
